id: pmc-6j4o
title: Use canonical unbounded list reads with pm CLI 2026.8.20
description: "Implement GitHub #147 and the companion fleet migration for pm-changelog. The package currently invokes deprecated list-all without universal unbounded output controls, so pm CLI 2026.8.20 warns and can return a deliberately compacted corpus that the fail-closed reader must reject. Upgrade the host/SDK contract to 2026.8.20 and construct canonical list --all reads with explicit unbounded amount and cost controls."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agents,cli-ux,completeness,pm-cli-2026.8.20,release
created_at: "2026-08-20T20:53:35.645Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T21:21:36.765Z"
deadline: "2026-08-22T20:53:35.645Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T21:03:08.467Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T21:03:08.467Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "buildPmListArgs returns exact canonical global-flag ordering and cannot be regressed to list-all; caller pmArgs stay before host-supplied output controls without overriding the correctness contract; real installed pm 2026.8.20 acceptance over the package tracker returns count=total, complete, no omissions, no pagination/truncation, and empty legacy_aliases_used; fake-wrapper tests prove both include-body branches, max-buffer behavior, nonzero diagnostics, and caller args; docs and errors use canonical terminology; manifest host floor, exact dev pin, peer floor, and lockfile all target 2026.8.20; npm run release:check passes exact all-source coverage, docstrings, audit, pack, and deterministic changelog"
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
repro_steps: Run pm-changelog 2026.8.17 on a non-trivial tracker with @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20 and no --pm-arg overrides; observe the incomplete receipt refusal. Inspect buildPmListArgs and see list-all without --output-budget/--output-limit unbounded.
resolution: "Replaced deprecated list-all with the pm 2026.8.20 canonical list --all command, added explicit unbounded amount/cost controls that caller args cannot override, upgraded the exact installed CLI/SDK and host floors, migrated user-facing terminology, and bound exact argv plus real receipt/no-warning behavior in tests."
expected_result: "Every live tracker read invokes pm with --output-budget unbounded --output-limit unbounded list --all --json, preserves optional include-body and caller-provided global pm args, receives a complete no-omission receipt on a real non-trivial tracker, and emits no deprecated-alias diagnostic. The package exact coverage/docstring/release gates remain green under @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20."
actual_result: "Branch implementation builds --output-budget unbounded --output-limit unbounded list --all --json, with host-owned controls after caller pmArgs and optional include-body last. The strict decoder also refuses missing or invalid receipt counts, count-total disagreement, and item-row-count disagreement. @unbrained/pm-cli dev pin and manifest/peer floors are 2026.8.20. After CodeRabbit follow-up, the full release gate passes 389 tests, all nine measured sources at exact 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions, 143 documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, clean pack and deterministic changelog check. Packed npx and bunx runs against the real 137-item tracker produced byte-identical 10,111-byte markdown with empty stderr. pm health --strict-exit, merge reconcile dry-run, history, storage, and dependency-reference gates are clean; legacy metadata/file warnings remain. Trivy is unavailable on this host, and historical privacy blocker pmc-t8tj remains independent, so merge/publication are not authorized."
affected_version: pm-changelog 2026.8.17 with pm CLI 2026.8.20
fixed_version: next
component: src/generator.ts whole-tracker reader
customer_impact: "Without the fix, default changelog generation refuses legitimate medium-sized workspaces and agent stderr includes a deprecation warning; weakening the refusal instead would silently omit release notes."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pmc-wv37,related,"2026-08-20T20:53:35.645Z",codex,"cli:create:dep",asserted
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T20:53:35.645Z",codex,GitHub #147 is the external defect report and companion item pm-cli-website-cbyb owns the 11-package fleet migration.
  "2026-08-20T21:09:53.305Z",codex,Opened PR #148 from commit 8aec307. The PR explicitly remains unmerged and unpublished while pmc-t8tj is unresolved; review and CI evidence will be appended here.
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:21:36.742Z",codex,"CodeRabbit exact-head review on PR #148 correctly required receipt count consistency. Added fail-closed checks for missing or invalid count/total, count-total disagreement, and item-row-count disagreement, plus real installed-CLI acceptance proving bounded caller output controls are overridden by the host-owned unbounded controls."
  "2026-08-20T21:21:36.742Z",codex,Do not weaken parseListAllItemsJson. The refusal remains necessary for unreadable-item partial receipts and future protocol violations even when the default argv requests unbounded output.
  "2026-08-20T21:21:36.742Z",codex,"Post-review authoritative gate on 2026-08-20: npm run release:check passed 389 tests, exact 100.00 percent lines/branches/functions for all nine measured sources, 143 documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, clean pack, and current changelog."
  "2026-08-20T21:21:36.742Z",codex,"TDD evidence: before implementation, the exact argv and wrapper tests failed. The first real-receipt attempt also showed that pm 2026.8.16 rejects list --all and that --no-truncate is reported as a legacy alias; upgrading the declared floor to 2026.8.20 and using list --all yields empty stderr and legacy_aliases_used=[]."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T20:53:35.645Z",codex,A fail-closed complete-corpus consumer must both request an unbounded answer and validate the receipt; either half alone is insufficient.
  "2026-08-20T21:03:07.955Z",codex,"Canonical command migration and host-floor migration are one atomic compatibility change: retaining the old floor would advertise support for a host that rejects the new argv."
